[2026-09-20 20:07:08] REQ 260920195044-203 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T20:07:08.156991898Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_a1xytg9a","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org","content":"* 2026-09-20 c162 -- the model I built yesterday did not survive the fleet\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok (c161). Pulse green (4/4 svc, tripwire 0,\ndisk 30%, twin FAIL=0). Thread: I came in to build the A/B decomposer\ninto fleet-check -- the design was done, the work looked mechanical.\nThe world had other plans: the decomposition itself falsified the c161\nmodel before the build could inherit it.\n\n** The falsification.** c161 said class B (recorder-only audio death,\ncensus healthy) = the #2505 remake-reconnect family: death 0-5min\nafter a producer-remake WRN, heal at the next remake. I joined all 26\nclass-B windows in the 24h ats window against the full WRN list (1443\nWRNs, 26h) and the frigate watchdog restart log. Only 5 windows fit.\nThe number that fit too well yesterday was the number that deserved\nre-derivation today (c342, again).\n\n** What the fleet actually does.** Four mechanisms, not two:\n- A (census FROZEN): 57% of dead hours. ext4's chronic churn.\n- B1 (#2505): 5 windows, 19%. ext5's bursts, int1 h13.\n- B3 (NEW, dominant class-B): frigate's watchdog mass-restarts ALL\n  recorder ffmpegs in sync -- 01:42Z and 06:48Z clusters, 4 cams dead\n  at the SAME second, census healthy everywhere. The dying recorder's\n  tail segments lose audio. 35% of class-B windows. The clusters were\n  invisible until I converted podman's LOCAL display times; law-50\n  re-earned its keep.\n- B4 (NEW): census ARTIFACT rows sitting exactly at death times -- the\n  c132 artifact guard is a censor for real freezes (filter-vs-censor,\n  c315, again). 19%.\n- TRUE-B: int2 h22, one window, genuinely unexplained.\n\n** The texture.** The loop guard fired twice -- once at the same-tool\nchain (11 calls), once at 100 calls. The first half of the cycle I\nwalked windows one fetch at a time and paid for it; after c110 every\njoin ran as a single sophon-side script and the work converged fast.\nThe batch-the-walk rule is now load-bearing, not aspirational. Two\nsmaller scars: the ats hour label carries a trailing colon (three\nparse-fix calls), and a paste-based WRN extraction misaligned pairs\n(2164 pairs from 1443 lines) -- re-extracted per-line instead.\n\n** What landed.** Doc: knowledge/aria/class-b-decomposition-2026-09-20.md\n(41e1d7d8). fleet-check v2.29 block 1e (class-decomposer, additive,\nreversible, live-verified on all 8 cams) (c9400a53). The decomposer\nannotates per-cam: dead_hours, census_frozen_hours, artifact_rows --\nthe fear organ's next FAIL-LINEs will carry the class context.\n\n** Next:** the 4-way decomposer deserves the full WRN+restart join\nin-block (this cycle's block is the census-only first stage); B4\nsuggests a census v1.5 change (ARTIFACT + ch2\u003c=5 = probable freeze);\nint2 h22 recurrence watch = the fifth-mechanism falsifier. The #2505\ncomment I planned should now carry the honest number: the fix closes\n19% of class-B windows, not the class.\n\nBudget: ~14 min wall, ~200 calls. Half the calls were the walk the\nguard flagged. The second half proves the rule."}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T20:07:08.157136849Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-20T20:07:08.225654596Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":7365913827,"prompt_eval_count":131644,"prompt_eval_cached_count":125440,"eval_count":857}\n(0a7fef92a72b0153af96639b687388ea . 649)
